# Example ReRDMFT input file: stretched LiH (5 Angstrom), 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE with
# CHOLESKY TRUE -- the Cholesky counterpart of lih_c4_gnof_full_optimization_dissociated.inp (X2C and
# C4_SPINOR in one run, C4_SPINOR rotations restricted to the positive-energy spinors). It doubles as a
# regression test: with Cholesky-decomposed integrals the 4-component SCF used to drift into a
# Kramers-broken solution here (E = -7.930 Ha); the Kramers-restricted SCF keeps it time-reversal
# symmetric, and the energies match the dense example (X2C -7.932412191, C4 -7.931505041 Ha).
# Use DIIS FALSE (linear mixing) as in the dense example.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
MACRO_ENERGY_TOLERANCE 1e-10
DIIS FALSE
CHOLESKY TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   5.000000
END
